{%- comment -%}
  compare-bar.liquid — the compare tray.

  Rendered statically from theme.liquid on every page, the same reasoning as
  the cart drawer and quick view: any product card anywhere can add to it, so
  it has to exist everywhere rather than living on one template.

  Starts hidden. Comparison is entirely client-side state (§16's localStorage
  ban is scoped to anything the cart depends on — this is neither the cart
  nor anything the server needs back), so a shopper who has never touched the
  feature sees nothing at all, ever: <compare-tray> only removes `hidden`
  once it finds something in storage to show.
{%- endcomment -%}

<compare-tray
  class="compare-tray"
  hidden
  data-remove-label="{{ 'products.product.compare_remove_label' | t | escape }}"
>
  <div class="compare-tray__inner page-width">
    <p class="compare-tray__count">
      <span data-compare-count>0</span>
      <span>{{ 'products.product.compare_label' | t }}</span>
    </p>

    {%- comment -%}
      Visible sibling to the aria-live announcement CompareToggle already
      fires when the 3-item cap is hit. The live region is real for a screen
      reader, but it is visually hidden by definition — a sighted shopper
      who clicks a 4th product's compare button sees nothing happen at all
      without this. Starts hidden; <compare-tray> shows it for a few seconds
      on a `compare:full` event and hides it again, it never needs its own
      permanent space reserved.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="compare-tray__notice" data-compare-notice hidden></p>

    <ul class="compare-tray__chips" data-compare-list></ul>

    <div class="compare-tray__actions">
      <button type="button" class="button--tertiary" data-compare-clear>
        {{ 'products.product.compare_clear' | t }}
      </button>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="button button--primary"
        data-drawer-toggle
        aria-controls="compare-drawer"
        aria-expanded="false"
        disabled
      >
        {{ 'products.product.compare_open' | t }}
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</compare-tray>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.compare_bar.name"
}
{% endschema %}
